1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:05,570
Families arrive in Kochi with someone they love in a hospital bed.

2
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:08,090
None of them are looking for a holiday.

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:09,610
They're looking for certainty.

4
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:12,289
This is how The Veedu goes to market to give it to them.

5
00:00:13,039 --> 00:00:15,899
Five stages of research came down to one insight.

6
00:00:15,949 --> 00:00:21,489
Distance is why families choose a stay, and it's the fact listings state least consistently.

7
00:00:21,539 --> 00:00:24,589
That one finding drives every decision that follows.

8
00:00:25,339 --> 00:00:27,159
So we don't go to market everywhere.

9
00:00:27,209 --> 00:00:30,709
We start with one hospital, Aster Medcity, and one customer:

10
00:00:30,759 --> 00:00:33,989
an out-of-town family caring for a patient who's admitted.

11
00:00:34,039 --> 00:00:38,350
More people than the hospital room allows, staying longer than a typical guest.

12
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,510
Our position is simple.

13
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:44,130
The Veedu is the stay-finder that checks what caregivers decide on:

14
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:50,910
the walking time to the hospital entrance, the all-in price for the whole family, and whether a place works for weeks.

15
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,350
Not near the hospital.

16
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,535
Checked, and dated.

17
00:00:54,285 --> 00:00:55,805
That promise is the brand.

18
00:00:55,855 --> 00:00:57,185
Calm, local, honest.

19
00:00:57,235 --> 00:00:59,295
Checked, so you don't have to.

20
00:00:59,345 --> 00:01:02,185
Which means the first marketing task isn't an ad.

21
00:01:02,235 --> 00:01:04,454
It's removing any claim we can't yet prove.

22
00:01:05,204 --> 00:01:07,324
Pricing follows the same logic.

23
00:01:07,374 --> 00:01:12,304
For a caregiver, the real price is time, effort and risk, so families pay nothing.

24
00:01:12,354 --> 00:01:16,774
Hosts list free during the pilot, then pay twelve percent on confirmed stays:

25
00:01:16,824 --> 00:01:19,601
less than the big platforms, and only when it works.

26
00:01:20,351 --> 00:01:22,961
Every message climbs from feature to benefit.

27
00:01:23,011 --> 00:01:24,871
A measured walking time becomes:

28
00:01:24,921 --> 00:01:26,531
you can reach your mother in minutes.

29
00:01:26,581 --> 00:01:28,201
One all-in price becomes:

30
00:01:28,251 --> 00:01:30,161
no surprise at checkout.

31
00:01:30,211 --> 00:01:33,840
This is a high-stakes decision, so we lead with evidence, not hype.

32
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:36,130
We go where the need shows up.

33
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:38,730
Search, when a family types the hospital's name.

34
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:40,680
WhatsApp, where they actually decide.

35
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:44,210
Walk-time videos, filmed from the hospital gate to every door.

36
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:46,940
And answer-ready pages for AI search.

37
00:01:46,990 --> 00:01:48,490
Social media supports.

38
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:49,521
It doesn't lead.

39
00:01:50,271 --> 00:01:51,901
The launch is soft on purpose.

40
00:01:51,951 --> 00:01:55,051
Ten to fifteen properties, every one checked in person.

41
00:01:55,101 --> 00:01:58,351
A short pre-launch to fix the site and verify supply.

42
00:01:58,401 --> 00:02:03,090
Then go live, watch every enquiry, and fix fast, because first impressions stick.

43
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:11,040
The pilot budget is about twenty-five thousand rupees, built ground-up from a target of forty qualified enquiries.

44
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:14,040
That's an assumption, and the cost per stay will start high.

45
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:17,075
We treat it as the price of learning, not a growth engine.

46
00:02:17,825 --> 00:02:19,455
The real engine is a loop.

47
00:02:19,505 --> 00:02:21,705
Every checked stay produces better data.

48
00:02:21,755 --> 00:02:23,635
Better data ranks and earns trust.

49
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:26,575
Trust brings more families, and more hosts.

50
00:02:26,625 --> 00:02:31,663
Over time, that dataset of verified facts becomes the moat a copycat can't buy.

51
00:02:32,413 --> 00:02:35,133
It all runs on a ninety-day plan with two gates.

52
00:02:35,183 --> 00:02:36,063
Prepare.

53
00:02:36,113 --> 00:02:37,163
Soft launch.

54
00:02:37,213 --> 00:02:38,173
Grow the loop.

55
00:02:38,223 --> 00:02:39,383
Then monetise.

56
00:02:39,433 --> 00:02:42,186
Money is committed only after each gate is passed.

57
00:02:42,936 --> 00:02:44,306
That's the go-to-market.

58
00:02:44,356 --> 00:02:45,456
One hospital.

59
00:02:45,506 --> 00:02:46,466
One promise.

60
00:02:46,516 --> 00:02:47,806
One loop.

61
00:02:47,856 --> 00:02:49,755
Win it honestly, then earn the next.
